        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the HMAC initialization functions temporarily overriding the digest value in the transformation context when they called the SHA initialization function, which reset the digest value. This led to incorrect HMAC computations under heavy load, as the digest value was not preserved during concurrent operations.

        Commit message:
        crypto: inside-secure - move the digest to the request
 context

This patches moves the digest information from the transformation
context to the request context. This fixes cases where HMAC init
functions were called and override the digest value for a short period
of time, as the HMAC init functions call the SHA init one which reset
the value. This lead to a small percentage of HMAC being incorrectly
computed under heavy load.

